     7	### 1. The only `MISS` grades a hedged example the next paragraph walks back, and pays it with a truncated bundle
     8	
     9	**Location:** ledger, first object row — “Reversed. All sixteen nuclear chromosomes of yeast synthesised… no orchestration of traits in fetuses”; “Where he was worst”: “He got the order of difficulty backwards.”
    10	
    11	**Problem:** The Lem sentence is: a better theory will let us “control evolution, change the speed and range of an organism’s regenerative potential, or orchestrate genetic traits in fetuses. All this will turn out to be possible long before, *say*, we gain the ability to create the chromosome apparatus of a nucleus in an artificial manner” (p. 193). Two sentences later in the same section he writes that “one should not take on an additional risk by predicting any future development of individual sciences” (p. 193). The chapter’s own method note, unquoted, is “We shall never say that things will be a certain way, only that they can be a certain way” (p. 185).
    12	
    13	The 2026 cell then collapses the first bundle to the one item that failed (fetal orchestration) and treats Sc2.0’s sixteen separately synthesised-and-characterised yeast chromosomes as the nuclear apparatus. That is the same truncation family as the retired Gibson `HIT`. As of the 2023 Cell special issue the consortium had all sixteen chromosomes built and a strain with *over half* a synthetic genome; they had not put the apparatus of one nucleus into one cell. Directed evolution (Arnold) and CRISPR are live forms of “control evolution”; they arrived before, not after, those chromosomes. He Jiankui (2018) is a crude, failed attempt to write a trait into human embryos and is not mentioned. A 2025 society *call* for a moratorium is evidence the germline path is live enough to brake, which is the opposite of §4 `MISS` (“no live path”).
    14	
    15	`MISS` on “A long before B” is not earned when A is a three-item “or” list partly realised, B is incomplete, the adverb is “say,” and the next paragraph declines to predict individual sciences.
    16	
    17	**Fix:** Drop the row, or narrow it to the one comparison that can be scored (fetal-trait *orchestration* vs a finished synthetic nucleus) and mark it `OPEN` or `EARLY`. If a negative is needed, use a claim he did not walk back (finding 3).
    18	
