    36	
    37	- **p. 188, own voice:** “as long as the number of variables is small, digital modeling works well. On increasing their number, this method quickly reaches the limit of its applicability. The modeling approach therefore has to be replaced by a different one.” Climate models, molecular dynamics, and learned models scaled digital methods instead of replacing them. Prior panels were right that *parameters ≠ Lem’s selected variables* and that the surrounding sentence is about modeling *all* variables. That is a reason to write the row carefully, not a reason to omit the only “this method has to be replaced” sentence in the chapter.
    38	- **p. 192 talent matrices:** he treats comprehensive knowledge of “the genetic codes that enact particular talents” as what unlocks embedding musical or mathematical talent in any egg. The live 2026 practice is selection among embryos already made (`embryo-screening-2024`), not a code-table write. “Where he was worst” already names this as the same shape of error; the ledger leaves it out because the antecedent is unmet. Unmet antecedent is `OPEN` for the *device*. The *mechanism* (cipher ⇒ trait) is `RIGHT QUESTION, WRONG ANSWER`.
